sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: fleet maintenance redesign (recipe.json read by Ansible, selected packages held). docs/cli/node/converge.mdx. Phases: input, agent, software, roles, tools, network, check; network applies hub first, then the Node and waits for the handshake.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: node:converge
  %% kind: node.converge
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane H icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>workflow execution
  participant N as Target Node<br/>reached over ssh
  participant H as VPN hub<br/>WireGuard peers
  CLI->>GW: node:converge NODE
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit node:converge NODE`
  %%> - syntax: `<node> [--base | --roles=a,b] [--idempotency-key=KEY] [--json]`
  Note over GW: Validate, reserve targets
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - access follows the [shared Node authority rule](/cli/node) (`NodeAccessAuthorizer`)
  %%> - admission uses recorded Node, role, Tool and network state; no live preflight
  %%> - Node convergence, role addition or convergence, enrollment and agent rekey share one Node admission lock; enrollment's role work stays inside its parent run
  alt unknown Node
    %% path: unknown-node
    GW--xCLI: Refused<br/>http.404
    %%> Result:
    %%> - no Operation, run or Node change
  else caller refused
    %% path: caller-refused
    GW--xCLI: Refused<br/>node_access.required
    %%> Result:
    %%> - no Operation, run or Node change
  else unsupported Node
    %% path: unsupported-node
    GW--xCLI: Refused<br/>node.converge_unsupported
    %%> Requirements:
    %%> - the target must be an active, managed Linux Node
    %%> Result:
    %%> - no Operation, run or Node change
  else selected role not assigned
    %% path: unassigned-role
    GW--xCLI: Refused<br/>validation.failed
    %%> Result:
    %%> - no Operation, run, role assignment or Node change
  else target or hub busy
    %% path: target-busy
    GW--xCLI: Refused<br/>operation.target_busy
    %%> Result:
    %%> - no new Operation or run; the existing holder keeps its reservation
  else admitted
    %% path: admitted
    opt --base
      %% path: base-scope
      Note over GW: Select base scope
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - narrows the admitted intent, without adding or removing assignments
    end
    opt --roles=a,b
      %% path: selected-roles
      Note over GW: Select recorded roles
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - narrows the admitted intent to the selected assignments
    end
    GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-node-converge
    %%> Inputs:
    %%> - target, scope, recorded roles, Tools, network and vault key names; playbooks read release pins
    %%> - the Gateway includes a CLI plan only for a Node with a recorded `ci-runner` assignment that is not being removed; scope flags do not change that decision
    %%> - reserve the Node and its recorded hub until the Operation settles
    GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>Operation ID
    %%> Result:
    %%> - execution continues asynchronously under the admitted Operation
    SW->>SW: Prepare the input<br/>phase: input
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - writes private inventory, vars and known_hosts from schema-validated inputs
    SW->>N: Install Orbit's layer<br/>Ansible phase: agent
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - applies the agent, Orbit-owned files and units, and the kernel policy (SCTP blocked, non-local bind); restarts only changed services
    %%> - with a CLI plan: requires and installs its pinned release and root profile
    %%> - without a CLI plan: needs no CLI release or probe; removes the managed `/usr/local/bin/orbit` link, regular `orbit-0.N.0` binaries and root profile at `/root/.orbit/config.json` in this phase, under the Node update lock; preserves unrelated executables, backups and directories
    SW->>N: Install pinned software<br/>Ansible phase: software
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - reads recipe.json and holds its selected packages at their pins
    SW->>N: Configure the roles<br/>Ansible phase: roles
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - repairs selected role configuration without changing an Instance or role assignment
    SW->>N: Apply recorded Tools<br/>Ansible phase: tools
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - runs the Tool helper once on the Swamp Node, before it judges a Tool
    %%> On a helper that cannot run:
    %%> - fail the phase and mark no Tool failed
    %%> On a Tool failure:
    %%> - continue with the other Tools and mark only that Tool failed
    alt recorded network in scope
      %% path: recorded-network
      SW->>H: Apply hub network<br/>Ansible phase: network
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - applies the recorded hub side before the peer; matching configuration is unchanged
      %%> - prunes only the peer files of Nodes that are gone or being removed, decided when the prune runs: it keeps every Node of the snapshot and every file above the snapshot's newest Node id, so a task VM that joins while the run waits keeps its peer
      %%> - on the hub: carries the mark in `wg syncconf`, opens SSH on its LAN address to its /24, writes the source unit (`orbit-hub-source.service`), restarts it on change or drift, and checks that a marked packet to a public address leaves from the public endpoint address; an IPv4 endpoint the hub does not hold fails the phase with the assertion `vpn.endpoint_not_local`
      SW->>N: Apply peer, wait<br/>Ansible phase: network
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - when the rendered hub endpoint is the hub's LAN address, first proves that the kernel routes it directly from the Node's `lan_ip` and that an SSH host key there has the hub's recorded fingerprint; a failed proof fails the phase before any WireGuard change, with the assertion `node.hub_lan_unreachable` or `node.hub_lan_identity_mismatch`, with no fallback to the public endpoint
      %%> - a changed hub endpoint, read from the previous `orbit.peers`, moves in one detached job on the Node: it takes WireGuard packets only from the new endpoint's address while it runs (assertion `node.hub_switch_unpinned` when it cannot), installs the staged files, ends the old session and accepts only a handshake from after the move; without one, it puts the previous files back and loads them, and the phase fails with the assertion `node.hub_switch_no_handshake`; when `wg` does not load the new files, it puts the previous ones back at once, and the assertion is `node.hub_switch_load_failed`
      %%> - applies the recorded Node side and waits for the tunnel handshake
      %%> - both arrows are one phase; the peer arrow is only for a peer target
      %%> - a target hub is applied once; it requires every recorded peer on its interface (assertion `vpn.hub_peer_missing`) and waits only for the peers that had a handshake in the 120 seconds before the change, each for a handshake in the last 180 seconds, so an offline peer does not fail it
    else no recorded network in scope
      %% path: no-recorded-network
      Note over SW: Network: no peer change<br/>Ansible phase: network
      %%> Result:
      %%> - the phase has no recorded configuration or handshake to apply
    end
    SW->>N: Check the Node<br/>Ansible phase: check
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - checks the selected software, units and role configuration, plus the recorded tunnel; on a target hub, every recorded peer on its interface, with no handshake wait
    %%> - checks the pinned CLI only when the Gateway supplied a CLI plan; otherwise checks that the managed CLI files are absent
    %%> - all seven phases run in order, idempotently; an empty scope item needs no mutation
    opt phases completed or failed
      %% path: cleanup
      SW->>SW: Remove private run files
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - declared cleanup waits for Node work to stop and removes only this run's files
      %%> - preserve the original failure and expose incomplete cleanup; interruption proves no cleanup
    end
    alt end check passes
      %% path: succeeded
      SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal result
      %%> Result:
      %%> - the shared reader marks the Operation succeeded and records each Tool's result
      %%> - a repeat is another full run, not an admission skip; matching tasks report zero changes
    else a phase fails
      %% path: phase-failed
      SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code · failed step
      %%> Result:
      %%> - stop at the failed phase and mark the Operation failed; later phases do not run
      %%> - unreachable targets fail here, not at a live admission check
      %%> On the Node:
      %%> - completed and partial changes remain; no rollback and no Instance or assignment change
      %%> Retry:
      %%> - a new attempt starts at input and reapplies every phase safely
    end
  end
